a 3 step process:

1) find the save file and remove the ".e" suffix.  the game has now
    been restored.
2) cross your fingers
3) sacrifice 3 important mail messages to /dev/null

that's it, usually works for me ...

(note: the bug may have crept into the save file in which case the
game will have to be mercifully destroyed.)

